# diff-digital-exe's rulings (tests/differential/comp.zig `readRulings`): where
# old `vera --emit-exe`'s stderr differs from vera-next's by a native-codegen
# build remark only. One line per fixture: `<path> <clause>: why`. The
# contract of `--emit-exe` is the exit status, the stdout transcript, the
# diagnostics about the design and the files written (IEEE 1364-2005 §3.1,
# §4.1: the 4-state run is the specified behaviour); `--state=auto`'s note on
# how the old native codegen built is none of those. A ruled fixture agrees
# only while its tiebreak holds (tests/differential/comp/judge.zig
# `remarkTiebreak`): status equal, files equal, old's stderr with its build
# remark removed (`withoutRemarks`) equal to new's, and new's stdout meets the
# fixture's own transcript (its `.expected.txt` gold when it has one, else
# old's stdout). research/vbackends.md T1, Q1 Decision B.
verilog/03_lexical_conventions/ams_lexical_escaped_ascii.v build remark: IEEE 1364-2005 §3.1, §4.1 (4-state is the specified run): old --emit-exe's note on its --state=auto strategy; the 4-state executable has none
